---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const projects = (await getCollection('projects', ({ data }) => !data.draft)).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf()
);
---

<Base title="GregBenza.ai — where good ideas go to grow">
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Greg. For about a year now I've been building with AI nearly every day — some
    big projects, a lot of small ones, most of them more interesting than they had any
    right to be. This is where I show that work: not the polished-résumé version, the
    real thing, with the files and workflows that made it sitting right underneath.
  </p>
  <p>
    Here's the bet. Anyone can write the perfect résumé now — so showing your work is
    the credential that's left. This is mine: the projects and the methods, plus the
    parts of the life around them — the woods, the cooking, the practice.
  </p>
  <p>
    It's built to be useful, not admired. Every post is meant to hand you something you
    can actually run, and it's a conversation, not a monument — poke holes, tell me what
    you'd do differently, and the work gets better for it. There's no finished version;
    the site just keeps pace with wherever I've gotten to.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <p class="eyebrow">The log</p>
  {
    projects.length === 0 ? (
      <p>Nothing here yet — the census fills this in.</p>
    ) : (
      <ul class="project-list">
        {projects.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/projects/${p.id}/`}>
              <span class="title">{p.data.title}</span>
              <span class="blurb">{p.data.blurb}</span>
              <time datetime={p.data.date.toISOString()}>
                {p.data.date.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })}
              </time>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )
  }
</Base>

<style>
  .project-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .project-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .project-list a {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--space-3) 0;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .project-list .title {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .project-list .blurb {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }
  .project-list time {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }
</style>
